infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Pay the handshake once, not per request
  desc Keep-alive amortises the TCP+TLS setup a fresh connection re-pays on every call
  compares
    - label New connection per request
      children
        - label TCP handshake: 1 round-trip
          desc About 30 ms on a 30 ms link
        - label TLS handshake: 1-2 round-trips
          desc Another 30-60 ms before any data flows
        - label 60-90 ms setup every request
          desc Paid before a single payload byte moves
        - label 10 req/s = 10 handshakes/s
          desc The cost the legacy default quietly hides
    - label Keep-alive pool reuse
      children
        - label Handshake paid once
          desc Connection stays open after the response
        - label Near 0 ms setup per request
          desc Next call reuses the live TCP+TLS connection
        - label On and pooled by default in undici
          desc Legacy global agent keep-alives since Node 19 but untuned
        - label Size with connections, not Infinity
          desc Match the downstream's real capacity
theme
  palette #f43f5e #10b981
